From the accessibility audit:

{quote}
Grade input fields accept alphabet characters but no warning is given when the form is submitted. These characters are not valid and the data field defaults to 0.00. 
{quote}

And a usability issue:
{quote}
Grades over the maximum value, when added to the grade input are identified, but the error message is not near to the input field in which it refers to.
{quote}

While reviewing MDL-78528,  [~accountid:557058:2ed4e27a-dd41-4dd7-bc32-805fb5cdfb1c] raised the following accessibility issue:

{color:#c1c7d0}_Duplicate IDs for the "Save changes" buttons. Specifically, these are the following IDs that are duplicated:_{color}
 * {color:#c1c7d0}_fitem_id_submitbutton_{color}
 * {color:#c1c7d0}_id_submitbutton_{color}
 * {color:#c1c7d0}_id_error_submitbutton_{color}

 

While the resolution for this matter is scheduled for MDL-78566, it has been postponed to upcoming releases. To address this accessibility concern in the interim and prevent the occurrence of duplicated IDs for action buttons, we have proactively instituted this solution.

In the Matrix provider users are asked to set an access token and a refresh token. However, it does not appear that the refresh token is used when the auth token is expired.

By default in a Synapse server access tokens are set to not expire, however Synapse server admins can set a token expiry. This is returned in the field value of: expires_in_ms see: [https://spec.matrix.org/unstable/client-server-api/#post_matrixclientv3login]

So for example a request in the form of:
{code:java}
curl -XPOST -d '{"type":"m.login.password", "user":"@admin:my.synapse.server.com", "password":"super_strong_password", "refresh_token":true}' "https://my.synapse.server.com/_matrix/client/r0/login"{code}
Returns
{code:java}
{"user_id":"@admin:my.synapse.server.com","access_token":"zzz_YWRtqW4_CfcZDsWnWREOnAPhFkIZ_1xHkz8","home_server":"my.synapse.server.com","device_id":"CCBYPHOHHV","expires_in_ms":299975,"refresh_token":"zzz_YWRtaW4_UqKXCksKgNQbbtghSeCx_1bfyMu","well_known":{"m.homeserver":{"base_url":"https://my.synapse.server.com/"}}}% {code}
When a Synapse server returns:
{noformat}
401 Unauthorized` response: {"errcode":"M_UNKNOWN_TOKEN","error":"Invalid access token passed.","soft_logout":false}{noformat}
Then the refresh token should be used to generate a new access token AND refresh token (Refresh tokens are use once).

Something like this will get a new set of tokens
{code:java}
curl -XPOST -d '{"refresh_token": "syr_YWRtaW4_NkklScYzqsuFURnCIqjJ_2hZOLW"}' "https://synapse:8008/_matrix/client/r0/refresh"{code}
The returned value will look something like:
{code:java}
{"access_token":"syt_YWRtaW4_pLsErBoVVBtCXywKVAsG_3Pau22","refresh_token":"syr_YWRtaW4_FLEtIOEqBUODDUFAmYiG_1b9nZ5","expires_in_ms":300000}{code}
The tokens will then need to be stored and REPLACE the existing stored tokens.

